                <pb facs="0318" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9311/358b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-12T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 12,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>346. I am informed by the Chinese Minister that the proposal is made by his
                    Government that the Chinese Legation here and the American Legation and several
                    others in Peking be made embassies. A statement of your views by cable would be
                    welcomed by me.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
